course: dictionary
lesson: 600
title: Awake, awoke and wide awake
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Awake has two jobs. As a describing word, awake means not sleeping: «He lies awake feeling awful and says sorry at breakfast.» He is not asleep, and he cannot stop thinking about what he did.
explain: As a doing word, to awake or to awaken means to wake up, or to make someone wake up. You will mostly meet the other forms, awoke and awoken, in old-fashioned books and fairy tales.
explain: Wide awake means fully awake and alert, so your mind is ready to notice things around you. A driver must stay awake and alert on a long journey.
fact: Awake means not sleeping.
fact: To awake, or to awaken, means to wake up.
fact: Awoke is an old-fashioned past form, often found in stories.
fact: «Screens before bed keep your brain awake», so reading or calm sounds can help you fall asleep.
fact: «Until 1846, most surgery was done on patients who were awake», which is why operations were so frightening for people then.
exercise: «He lies awake feeling awful and says sorry at breakfast.» What does awake mean here? | *Not sleeping | Asleep and dreaming | Standing up | Very cheerful
exercise: What does wide awake mean? | *Fully awake and alert | Wide, like a very big bed | Yawning loudly | Sleeping with the eyes open
exercise: «Screens before bed keep your brain awake.» According to this text, what helps you fall asleep? | Loud music | Playing outside late | *Reading or calm sounds | Screens
test: In an old fairy tale, «The prince awoke at dawn.» What does awoke mean? | *Woke up | Fell asleep | Ran away | Ate his breakfast
test: «It is asleep, but only with half its brain: the other half stays awake to steer.» What does awake mean here? | Lost | *Not sleeping | Asleep | Dreaming happily
exam: «People sometimes feel pain in dreams, so pinching yourself is not complete proof that you are awake.» Why is pinching yourself not complete proof? | *Because people can feel pain in dreams | Because awake means asleep | Because you always fall asleep after pinching | Because pinching never hurts
